Wix, Squarespace, GoDaddy — website builders are everywhere, and they're tempting. But are they the right choice for your small business?

NC Digital builds custom websites that outperform website builders on speed, SEO, and conversions. Here's why it matters.

## Website builders vs custom web design

**Website builders** like Wix and Squarespace are designed to be quick and easy — but they come with trade-offs:

- Slower loading speeds (bad for SEO and user experience)
- Limited control over SEO settings
- Template-based designs that look generic
- Monthly subscription fees that add up over time
- Harder to migrate away from when you outgrow them

**Custom web design** from NC Digital gives you:

- A site built specifically for your business and customers
- Full control over SEO from day one
- Faster loading speeds
- No ongoing platform fees
- A site that grows with your business

## Which is right for you?

If you're just starting out and testing an idea, a website builder might be enough for now. But if you're a serious business that wants to rank on Google and generate leads — a custom-built website will outperform a builder every time.

[Get a free website plan](/free-website-plan/) and we'll show you exactly what a custom site would look like for your business.

## Frequently asked questions

**Are website builders bad for SEO?**

They're not terrible, but they're limited. Custom websites give you far more control over the technical SEO factors that matter most.

**How much more does a custom website cost?**

Less than you might think. [Get a free quote](/free-website-plan/) and compare it to your builder subscription over 2–3 years.
